 ```
 
+Footnotes are numbered and listed in the order in which they are first
+referenced in the document, regardless of the order in which their content is
+defined. Footnotes which are only referenced from within other footnotes follow
+those referenced in the body of the document, and any footnotes which are defined
+but never referenced are listed last, in the order they were defined. To number
+footnotes in the order of their definitions instead, set the
+`USE_DEFINITION_ORDER` option to `True`.
+
 Usage
 -----
 
